    "body": "Scheduled tasks must exist in the QIKVRT Digital Twin and stay synchronized with their executing scheduler. This PR adds the private durable schedule registry and extends the existing authenticated API shim with an event-driven bridge to the same existing executor ID.\n\nThe bridge performs authenticated source read \u2192 exact local revision/CAS and durable prepare \u2192 conditional update of the existing executor when required \u2192 fresh source readback \u2192 Twin reconcile \u2192 independent persisted local readback. Empty changes import source events without mutation. Stable event IDs bind the exact original request; redelivery freshly reobserves the source. No timer, polling loop, create operation, run-now operation or second executor is introduced.\n\nA private SQLite journal persists PREPARED and ATTEMPTED before the external call. Once attempted, an update is never blindly retried. Restart after an external effect or after reconcile can complete only from matching fresh source bytes. Journal revision advances atomically with reconcile. Drift, stale observations, contradictory versions, reordered/stale revisions, event collisions, concurrent bridge/manual writers and missing authentication fail closed.\n\nThe server-configured HttpScheduleExecutor uses scoped, expiring credentials, bounded closed JSON, no redirects and exact repository/principal binding. Mutations require atomic CAS in the source executor's authority domain (If-Match plus stable idempotency key). The currently exposed ChatGPT automations.update tool has no conditional version argument; a gateway using only that operation must advertise conditional_update=false and remains observation-only. The adapter contract does not claim that such a productive CAS gateway or event carrier is already installed.\n\nThe supported calendar remains bounded hourly/daily/weekly with IANA timezone binding, gap skipping, first-fold semantics and explicit UTC recurrence. Existing private task prompts and credentials remain outside public Git. PR #422's separate Digital Twin/reference-model and promotion-test repairs are unchanged.\n\nValidation of the published successor:\n\n- HEAD: `b284dd0946c5147a0d3f4a38a2361df339c1738e`; TREE: `b352276338e92b46c536686fb89fcd57aeccdbd1`.\n- Parents: previous PR head `1bd9f15c70f62387829f2d24d3b7b3dbc61ceb76` and freshly observed Main `469a95ac4ef14692dda69673b8a75eb2cf03685d`. Main's six lifecycle paths were integrated without history rewriting.\n- `make test`: exit 0 on the actual GitHub-created commit; 566 Python test executions and 7,864,387 C90 effect-ack checks; clean working tree.\n- 39 scheduling regressions cover restart before/after effect and after reconcile, ambiguous/lost acknowledgement, reordering, same-event replay, simultaneous writers, source CAS conflict, pause/resume, DST fold/gap, authentication, stale/conflicting source observations and independent local readback.\n- Real local HTTP test flow: existing shim \u2192 authenticated test gateway \u2192 existing-task conditional PATCH \u2192 fresh GET \u2192 SQLite reconcile/readback. This is test evidence, not productive external verification.\n- Integrity: 3,920 classified entries and 3,911 immutable digests verified. All 16 materialized changed blobs and the resulting GitHub tree exactly matched the locally tested bytes.\n- The existing historical finalizer fixture required restoring commit `56127a6fd7dadea331fea98ed6cba19b4b96c6b2` from an existing local repository; its unchanged 8-test suite passed. No test or gate was bypassed.\n\nThe earlier real regulatory-watch roundtrip for task `6abe3d7a68c88191aee2117043e08cde` remains historical evidence in the binding/work-unit record. It is not transferred to this successor as productive continuous-bridge proof.\n\nAcceptance boundary: `local_dispatch_authorized=false`, `continuous_bridge_verified=false`, and `effect_ack_done=false`. Actual authenticated provider CAS, source-event/restart delivery to the deployed Twin, productive fresh source/local readback and drift witnesses remain unverified. Independent Code Owner review and Main integration remain separate. No deployment, duplicate executor, notification delivery, Authority/Mirror equality or general EFFECT_ACK_DONE is inferred.\n\nThe work unit preserves Ingolf Lohmann's requirement, Codex's implementation contribution, reuse inventory, exact source bindings and remaining runtime boundary. The next productive step is binding an actual authenticated source-domain CAS gateway and existing-source event carrier, followed by fresh deployed-subject restart/redelivery and drift readback. Ordinary automations.update alone cannot establish the required atomic conditional-write guarantee.\n\nFresh hosted readback: [Exact-head QIKVRT CI run 36873505827](https://github.com/ingolf-lohmann/qik-vrt/actions/runs/36873505827) completed SUCCESS for HEAD `b284dd0946c5147a0d3f4a38a2361df339c1738e`, including full tests, same-writer successor re-entry and terminal tested-fixpoint enforcement. Final PR readback is OPEN, non-draft and mergeable against Main `469a95ac4ef14692dda69673b8a75eb2cf03685d`; no native review was present.\n\nThe separate trusted-Main [review-gate publisher run 36873531797](https://github.com/ingolf-lohmann/qik-vrt/actions/runs/36873531797) published `QIKVRT requested review execution=failure` for this exact head, with `first_blocker=CODE_OWNER_RULE_NOT_ENFORCED`: Main must require one approval, Code Owner review, stale-review dismissal and last-push approval. Publisher-job SUCCESS is observation success, not gate success. This governance blocker remains outside this scheduling extension; no merge or general completion is claimed.\n\nRemote-exact local test-log SHA-256: `8f8902e9323b1d0f3029d90c1fb1f494f9d1a53063c7c1ee2f3d5041bbaa0237`.",
